@fire I have still not managed to get any frame decoded and presented yet, bu the infrastructure seems mostly there for it. Now that there's at least one windows editor build are you able to test what happens on your machine? Also if you can do you have any hardware which supports `queryResultStatusSupport` (as reported by `vulkaninfo`)? Mine doesn't which is why I haven't implemented success queries yet but if you have something which does it could help with debugging.

An interesting thing I found about matroska is that each NAL unit is prefixed by it's size (32-bit) and has no Annex B start code (which vulkan seemingly requires). Both krita and kdenlive had this behaviour so either they both use the same buggy encoder or this is just a part of the matroska standard.

Beyond that the results I get from decoding the H.264 stream and what I get from entering it into https://media-analyzer.pro/app seems close enough. For my high profile test video I overread 1 byte of the SPS and for my baseline test video (which I have tested far less rigorously) it overreads 2 bytes of the PPS. Hopefully neither of those cause signifant issues
